{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "364c0e8d-4dcb-4e76-923c-b13124767827",
    "name": "Soosky Storm API - Cone not_available mock",
    "description": "Collection de fake deterministic truong hop cone not_available.\n\nCach dung:\n1. Import collection nay vao Postman.\n2. Tao Mock Server tu collection va chon Public. Request 'NHC source mock > CurrentStorms.json (response fake)' da co response example.\n3. Copy URL Mock Server, sau do dat tren backend: NHC_CURRENT_STORMS_URL=<mock-url>/CurrentStorms.json.\n4. Restart backend (npm start).\n5. Chay request 'Backend verification > Cone is not_available'.\n\nMock co storm nhc:AL052025 ton tai trong activeStorms, nhung co y khong co trackCone. Vi vay backend phai tra 200 va data.availability = not_available. Postman khong the tu thay doi bien moi truong cua backend; buoc 3 phai thuc hien trong file .env cua backend dang chay.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:3001",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "stormId",
      "value": "nhc:AL052025",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "mockBaseUrl",
      "value": "https://your-mock-server.mock.pstmn.io",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "NHC source mock",
      "description": "Tao Postman Mock Server tu collection nay. Mock Server can public de backend co the goi ma khong can x-api-key.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "CurrentStorms.json (response fake)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{mockBaseUrl}}/CurrentStorms.json",
            "description": "Response example ben duoi la du lieu ma backend can doc. Storm co forecastTrack bat buoc, nhung khong co trackCone."
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "200 - active storm without cone",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{mockBaseUrl}}/CurrentStorms.json",
                  "host": [
                    "{{mockBaseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "CurrentStorms.json"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [
                {
                  "key": "Content-Type",
                  "value": "application/json"
                }
              ],
              "cookie": [],
              "body": "{\n  \"activeStorms\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"al052025\",\n      \"name\": \"Test Storm\",\n      \"classification\": \"TS\",\n      \"intensity\": \"50\",\n      \"latitudeNumeric\": 22.3,\n      \"longitudeNumeric\": -70.2,\n      \"lastUpdate\": \"2025-09-01T00:00:00.000Z\",\n      \"forecastTrack\": {\n        \"issuance\": \"2025-09-01T00:00:00.000Z\",\n        \"kmzFile\": \"https://example.test/track.kmz\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Backend verification",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Cone is not_available",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns HTTP 200', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(200));",
                  "pm.test('returns success envelope', () => pm.expect(body.ok).to.equal(true));",
                  "pm.test('cone availability is not_available', () => pm.expect(body.data.availability).to.equal('not_available'));",
                  "pm.test('cone has no geometry', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data.geometryKind).to.equal(null);",
                  "    pm.expect(body.data.geojson).to.equal(null);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('includes a reason', () => pm.expect(body.data.reason).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/storms/{{stormId}}/cone",
            "description": "Chay sau khi backend da duoc cau hinh NHC_CURRENT_STORMS_URL tro toi Postman Mock Server."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
